From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 11:25:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: drm/msm/dsi: log the raw error registers

Not for source= beyond the investigation it belongs to.

dsi_err_worker() prints err_work_state and nothing else, which collapses
six registers into six bits -- and each handler clears its register
before anyone can read it. So the only thing that ever reaches the log
is "dsi_err_worker: status=5", which is not enough to tell a real fault
from a benign one.

It is worse than merely coarse. dsi_fifo_status() raises
DSI_ERR_STATE_FIFO for *any* non-zero FIFO_STATUS, and that register
carries DLN0_LP_FIFO_EMPTY, DLN0_HS_FIFO_EMPTY and the same for lanes
1-3 -- an idle FIFO is empty, so those bits are a normal condition
rather than an error. Part of "status=5" may be nothing at all.

Snapshot FIFO_STATUS, TIMEOUT_STATUS, ACK_ERR_STATUS, STATUS0,
DLN0_PHY_ERR and CLK_STATUS before the handlers run, and print them
ratelimited along with the CMD_MODE_MDP_BUSY and CMD_MODE_DMA_BUSY bits,
so the state of the link at the moment of the error is visible too.

Written for the glitched lines this panel paints while the brightness
ramps down under a repainting compositor, after three plausible fixes
were built, flashed and disproven: sending the brightness in LP instead
of HS, raising the DSI clock from 100% to 230% of the theoretical
minimum, and waiting for CMD_MODE_MDP_BUSY to clear before starting a
command DMA. None changed the artefact, and the last never timed out
once, so the contention theory behind it is unsupported. This stops the
guessing and asks the hardware instead.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -1684,6 +1684,29 @@
 
 static void dsi_error(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host)
 {
+	/*
+	 * DIAGNOSTIC. dsi_err_worker() only ever prints err_work_state, which
+	 * collapses six registers into six bits and is cleared by the handlers
+	 * below before anyone can look at it. "status=5" is therefore all the
+	 * information that reaches the log, and it is not enough to tell a real
+	 * fault from a benign one -- dsi_fifo_status() in particular raises
+	 * DSI_ERR_STATE_FIFO for *any* non-zero FIFO_STATUS, and that register
+	 * carries DLN*_FIFO_EMPTY bits, which are a normal idle condition.
+	 *
+	 * Snapshot the raw values before the handlers clear them.
+	 */
+	u32 d_fifo = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_FIFO_STATUS);
+	u32 d_tout = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_TIMEOUT_STATUS);
+	u32 d_ack = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_ACK_ERR_STATUS);
+	u32 d_stat = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_STATUS0);
+	u32 d_phy = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_DLN0_PHY_ERR);
+	u32 d_clk = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_CLK_STATUS);
+
+	pr_err_ratelimited("dsi-diag: fifo=%08x timeout=%08x ack=%08x status0=%08x phy=%08x clk=%08x mdp_busy=%d dma_busy=%d\n",
+			   d_fifo, d_tout, d_ack, d_stat, d_phy, d_clk,
+			   !!(d_stat & DSI_STATUS0_CMD_MODE_MDP_BUSY),
+			   !!(d_stat & DSI_STATUS0_CMD_MODE_DMA_BUSY));
+
 	/* disable dsi error interrupt */
 	dsi_intr_ctrl(msm_host, DSI_IRQ_MASK_ERROR, 0);
 
